# Upstream Kyverno ValidatingPolicies, vendored unchanged at one commit.
# Re-vendor with scripts/kyverno-vendor.sh; CI checks the sha256 lines.
# Renovate moves `commit:` (git-refs on main: the repo has no tags) and the
# renovate-render workflow re-vendors in the same pull request.
#
# The files keep upstream's validationActions. CI decides what blocks by
# policy name (scripts/ci/kyverno.sh); the cluster runs those in Deny, the
# rest in Audit (infrastructure/kyverno-policies).
#
# Not vendored, from best-practices-vpol:
#   require-labels             needs site configuration (the label set)
#   restrict-image-registries  needs site configuration (the registry list)
#   disallow-helm-tiller       no Tiller (Helm 2) anywhere
#   disallow-empty-ingress-host  the Tailscale Ingresses use defaultBackend by design
#   require-probes             errors on every CronJob (it matches cronjobs and
#                              reads object.spec.template) and accepts one probe
#                              of three; policies/kyverno/require-probes.yaml
#                              (readiness and liveness) stays instead
#   require-drop-cap-net-raw   matches an explicit CAP_NET_RAW or NET_RAW drop
#                              entry only, so it failed the stricter
#                              `drop: [ALL]` this repo sets everywhere (upstream
#                              says it "may not strictly conform to the Pod
#                              Security Standards"); policies/kyverno/
#                              drop-cap-net-raw.yaml, which counts ALL, stays
#                              instead
#
# Replaced homelab copies (same findings over deploy/ on 2026-10-16):
#   disallow-latest-tag  -> best-practices-vpol/disallow-latest-tag (it checks
#                           `containers` only; the image-digest rule of
#                           scripts/ci/repo_policy.py pins every image line)
#   disallow-privileged  -> pod-security-vpol/baseline/disallow-privileged-containers
#   require-resources    -> best-practices-vpol/require-pod-requests-limits
